Vendored from crates.io accesskit_unix 0.24.0 (AccessKit, MIT OR Apache-2.0).
Patched locally to expose deprecated AT-SPI Text boundary methods used by
Orca 42/libatspi 2.44, and preserve the struct argument in AT-SPI Cache
AddAccessible/RemoveAccessible signals, and forward bounded synchronous AT-SPI
keyboard events with registry listener tracking. Sources otherwise retain their upstream form.
Protected printable key lifecycles are withheld except for non-text-producing Ctrl/Super
chords or physically held Orca modifiers. Forwarded navigation/command key IDs and
hardware codes remain visible to AT-SPI bus clients with listener access.
Only one key request may be queued or in flight; its permit survives caller timeout.
